## 3. How we know

### [CXC-VISION-EPISTEMICS] How we know any of it works — machine signals routinely AGREE WITH THE WRONG ANSWER
- claim: Machine signals in this fleet do not merely go ABSENT — they routinely AGREE WITH THE WRONG ANSWER. That distinction is the whole pillar: an absent signal prompts investigation, an agreeing one closes it. At least six instances in one session, 2026-08-11/12.
- instance-capture-bmp: `capture.bmp` rendered PERFECTLY over a byte-swapped panel — it decodes the same buffer with the same endian assumption that WROTE it. Waveshare C6; resolved by `RAMCTRL` 0xE8 -> 0xE0. The image was well-formed, correct layout, correct-LOOKING palette.
- instance-spi-overclock: Raising SPI from 11.43 MHz to 40 MHz improved EVERY timing number while the display got WORSE — whole transactions were dropped, and the ABSENCE of tearing was the diagnosis. ~15 MHz is the datasheet ceiling. The results table reads like a success and is kept precisely for that reason.
- instance-mcp2515-init: `MCP2515 successfully initialized` with the interrupt line on the wrong GPIO. Init exercises SPI ONLY; the INT line is what delivers RX. A true statement about the wrong subsystem.
- instance-drop-counter: An allowlist drop counter reporting 0 because enforcement happened at SUBSCRIBE time, so the counter could not increment. Structurally pinned at zero.
- instance-bitrate-sweep: A listen-only bitrate sweep that read IDENTICALLY for "wrong bitrate" and "receive pin not connected" — an instrument whose output does not distinguish the two hypotheses it was run to distinguish.
- instance-twai-selftest: A TWAI loopback self-test that returned PASS and FAIL for the SAME binary on the SAME board. An unrepeatable test is not a measurement, and a board was declared good on the strength of one PASS.
- rule-self-verification: Any property read back THROUGH THE SAME ASSUMPTION THAT WROTE IT cannot be self-verified. This is the generator of the capture.bmp class, not a special case of it.
- rule-negative-control: An instrument that can only report SUCCESS is not an instrument. It needs a NEGATIVE CONTROL — a deliberate fault injector that makes it fail — proving its zero means something. The drop counter had none and its zero meant nothing.
- rule-needs-eyes: Colour order, endianness, GRAM offset, brightness and latched external state need EYES, always. No machine channel on these boards is independent of the assumption under test.
- rule-ask-specific-colours: When asking a human, ask about SPECIFIC colours. "Blue shows green, green shows red" is arithmetically a BYTE swap: RGB565 0x001F byte-swaps to 0x1F00 (G=56/63, green-dominant) and 0x07E0 to 0xE007 (R=28/31, red-dominant). A CHANNEL swap instead shows blue as RED. That one distinction turned an open-ended colour hunt into a one-bit fix, and it only works if the question names colours rather than asking whether it "looks right".
- rule-power-then-substrate-then-protocol: Prove POWER AT THE PART, then the SUBSTRATE, then the PROTOCOL. On 2026-08-12, three rounds of protocol diagnostics ran against a transceiver that had no supply.
- rule-port-paths-are-not-identities: Port paths changed FIVE times in one session. Match the full USB serial; never `esptool chip-id`, which resets the board — the reset is the exact harm the identity check was being run to avoid.
- rule-loopback-proves-nothing-about-peers: One node talking to itself proves the software and the adapter, and NOTHING about interoperation. A closed world cannot detect a layout disagreement with a different implementation, which is how [BP-CAN-ID-DIVERGENCE] stayed invisible.
- scope-of-this-pillar: These rules are drawn from EMBEDDED bring-up. They generalise to any place where the instrument shares an assumption with the thing measured — including this corpus's own tooling — but the six instances are all hardware, and that is the evidence base being claimed.
- decomposition-note: This node carries a catalogue of six instances AND eight rules. If either half starts being cited on its own, split it: the rules are the referenceable part and the instances are their evidence.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-VISION]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND], [BP-CAN-ID-DIVERGENCE], [CXC-CONFIG-BUS-VERIFIED], [CXC-BOARD-HW-SELF-CONFIRMING]

