## 4. Recovery and placement

### [CXC-VISION-RECOVERY] How an agent re-hydrates this — carry the QUERY, never the snapshot
- claim: This document exists to be FETCHED, not copied. An agent bootstrap must carry a QUERY, so the vision evolves in the corpus and every re-hydration picks up current state.
- failure-mode-this-prevents: A static copy inside an agent definition goes stale SILENTLY. It is the same disease as `CAN_BRIDGE_REGISTER`: a hand-maintained list that no longer matches the thing it describes and says nothing when it diverges. An agent quoting a superseded claim is INDISTINGUISHABLE from one quoting a current one.
- recovery-query-step-1: `lts_node(corpus="intelligence-console", node_id="CXC-VISION")` — the root, its 8 properties and its per-layer forward/reverse edges (edge_total 20).
- recovery-query-step-2: `lts_traverse(corpus="intelligence-console", start_node="CXC-VISION", max_depth=1, layers=["semantic"], direction="both")` — returns 10 nodes and 11 edges: this root, all seven pillars (which reach it by `PART_OF`), plus the two document roots the root cites.
- recovery-query-fallback: `lts_find(corpus="intelligence-console", text="CXC-VISION")` — total_matched 8, the whole family. Use this if a pillar id is ever renamed.
- parameter-names-are-load-bearing: ⛔ `start_node` and `max_depth`, NOT `start` and `depth`. The first draft of this node recorded the latter; the call raised `TypeError` and returned nothing. A bootstrap carrying that line would have re-hydrated silence and read it as an empty vision.
- token-budget-caveat: `lts_traverse` truncates against `token_budget` (default 32,768). At a small explicit budget the same call returns ONE node with `truncated: true` — which is indistinguishable from a vision with no pillars unless the caller reads the flag. Do not pass a small budget on the recovery path.
- corpus-id-is-not-the-directory-name: ⛔ The corpus id is `intelligence-console`, NOT `platform-specs`. There is no `platform-specs` entry in the corpus registry — `corpora/platform-specs` is registered as the `specs` AREA of the `intelligence-console` corpus, and `intelligence-console` has THREE live roots (so `lts_preview` refuses that corpus id as ambiguous and wants a directory path instead). A query naming `platform-specs` resolves to nothing and looks exactly like a corpus with no matching nodes.
- verified: All three calls were RUN against the live engine on 2026-08-13, after this file landed, and each returned the counts quoted above. Re-verify whenever a node id on this page changes.
- verify-before-recording: A recovery query that does not resolve is WORSE than none, because it LOOKS like coverage. Never record a query you have not executed — this node's own first draft named a corpus that does not exist AND two parameters that do not exist, and both were caught only by running them.
- consumers: Two agent bootstraps, re-hydrated at every session start.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-VISION]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND], [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]

