### [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT] Placement is UNRATIFIED — and this directory has two live filename-number collisions
- placement-status: UNRATIFIED. This document was written into `corpora/platform-specs/` because that is where its neighbours are, NOT because the placement was ruled. It is a synthesis across specs rather than a spec, so it may belong in a different corpus entirely.
- neighbours-also-unratified: `60-board-hardware-inventory.lts` and `61-config-over-bus.lts` are both already flagged `[PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED]`. Three consecutive files now carry the same flag, which is itself the signal that the placement question is overdue rather than pending.
- corpus-defect-61: RESOLVED 2026-08-17 — `61-fleet-console.lts` was renamed to `76-fleet-console.lts` (75 was already claimed by the worktrunk-cutover spec). All 40 `[CXC-FC-*]` node ids are unchanged, and every reference to the old filename was a DESCRIPTION of this collision rather than a citation, so nothing rotted. `61-config-over-bus.lts` keeps 61. ⚠ TWO collisions remain: `00-composer-design-principles.lts`/`00-composer-overview.lts` and `46-console-sources-on-the-bus.lts`/`46-handover-process.lts` — both left alone deliberately, because unlike 61 their filenames are REAL citations (17/25 and 8/10 referring files) and renaming would rot live pointers.
- corpus-defect-46: The same collision already exists at 46: `46-console-sources-on-the-bus.lts` AND `46-handover-process.lts`. Found while checking 61, and it is the older instance — so this is a recurring convention failure with no guard, not a one-off.
- why-git-will-never-flag-it: The FILENAMES differ, so there is no merge conflict, no duplicate path, and no VCS signal of any kind. The collision is in the CONVENTION, not in the filesystem — which is exactly the shape of failure the rest of this document is about: a hand-maintained ordering with no instrument watching it.
- also-present: `60-board-hardware-inventory.lts.bak` sits in the same directory. It is not a `.lts` file so the parser never reads it, but it is a second copy of a live document with no marker saying which is authoritative.
- do-not-renumber-unilaterally: The numeric prefix appears in sibling frontmatter `depends-on:` file lists and in prose citations across the corpus, so a rename is a corpus-wide edit rather than a `git mv`. The resolution is the architect's.
- suggested-guard: Whatever is decided, the durable fix is an instrument: a lint that fails when two `.lts` files in one corpus root share a numeric prefix. A convention nothing checks will collide again — it already has, twice.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-VISION]
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND], [SPEC:CXC-CONFIG-BUS]

